p.note('The page distinguishes ordinary cohomology H from several double-stemmed hypercohomology Hs, and a looped sheaf-style Ext from the ordinary Extq on the right. The functor inside the Ext expressions is Λ, not N: its two legs are separate from the following parenthesis. The theorem displays K(O,m) but bounds excess by n; this mismatch is retained. The right margin characteristic sign has a lower bar (p≥0), even though the opening formula works over Fp. The right margin degree m/n remains doubtful. The lower class has a retraced degree; its representing map to K(O,n) fixes n within the admitted shapes. The added star on F in the Illusie display is retained despite F having been called an abelian object.')
p.habit('On scan374 a doubled left H-stem is deliberate and occurs repeatedly in the derived/cohomological displays, but ordinary H also occurs. The two-leg Λ before an open parenthesis resembles N when the parenthesis is read as its third stroke; C does this three times. The looped prefix Cl. can resemble script A. Small m/n remains locally unsafe in the right margin; no universal identification is imposed. H normalizes several missing accents and supplies a close parenthesis to the unfinished margin map.')
